For anyone interested, this is where the removing happens (at tile_set_atlas_source_editor.cpp:1705):
```
void TileSetAtlasSourceEditor::shortcut_input(const Ref<InputEvent> &p_event) {
	// Check for shortcuts.
	if (ED_IS_SHORTCUT("tiles_editor/delete", p_event)) {
		print_line("Debug Removing 3");
		if (tools_button_group->get_pressed_button() == tool_select_button && !selection.is_empty()) {
			_menu_option(TILE_DELETE);
			accept_event();
		}
	}
}
```

I think there is a larger issue however, as the intended deletion of a tile only works when I click on a specific area in the editor. Most of the time pressing delete will create a prompt to remove the tile map node/delete the tile map file.
